 - HOST GATES: final macOS focused pytest exited 0 with 141 passed; full pytest exited 0 with 1159 passed / 21 skips; the wheel-installed native Go 1.25.5 fixture exited 0 with 10 passed. Configured and Linux-target strict mypy passed 65 files; unsupported-Linux focused selection passed 129 / skipped 12; build, Twine, compileall, tabnanny, and diff hygiene exited 0.
 - QUALIFICATION BOUNDARY: `ssh lev` timed out with exit 255 and no local Linux container runtime was available, so no native Linux full-suite claim is made. The invalid whole-suite Darwin kernel emulation and every iterative non-zero gate remain recorded as failures in `TASK-260720-2g21eg_cycle6-ci-portability-rework.md`.
+
+### 2026-07-30 — Runtime reuse and immutable built-command activation handoff
+- DEVELOPER: `TASK-260720-11yhth` preserves the CocoaSkills worktree at base `11160f642d65a8daf3fbcca5401dca5ec80440f9`. The unstaged task delta is limited to `src/csk/shims.py`, narrow `global_bins.py` / `installer.py` wiring, `tests/test_shims.py`, and new `tests/test_build_activation.py`; no shell-profile code, stage, commit, or push was introduced.
+- HARDENING: commit-keyed script runtime reuse now validates every required active command as a contained regular file and replaces incomplete state through staging. Project, global, and user-bin launchers share one command namespace; built commands target validated immutable cache artifacts without executing them during install.
+- DEFECTS CLOSED: Windows launcher writes no longer pass through planted symlinks or produce translated `CR CR LF`; `.cmd` command names survive stale-shim cleanup; Windows wrappers clear a shadowing `ERRORLEVEL` variable, quote the executable, forward `%*`, and reject command/path injection.
+- GATES: recovery verification ran focused pytest at exit 0 with 100 passed / 6 Windows-only skips, strict mypy at exit 0 over 65 files, task Ruff, compileall, package build, Twine, diff hygiene, and the no-`uv.lock` check at exit 0. Attached native Windows evidence records 7 targeted execution tests passing and the full suite excluding one unrelated PowerShell-policy test at 852 passed / 183 skipped / 1 deselected.
+- ANOMALY: the native Windows host blocks all `.ps1` files through CurrentUser execution policy, so the unrelated shell-init test remains expected-red there; host strict mypy also reports pre-existing platform-stub errors outside the touched files. A handoff-time read-only SSH probe timed out with exit 255, so the task-scoped remote directory could not be removed.

